00:00:03.189 --> 00:00:05.030 align:start position:0%
nowadays the majority of the european  population lives in cities  and urbanization is further on the  increase  the quality of life in cities is  hindered by the environmental challenges  linked to increasing urbanization  this is why the european commission has  launched the green city accord  air pollution is the main environmental  cause of premature death  and disease the eu's air quality  standards continue to be exceeded  in over 100 cities securing clean and  safe water for a growing urban  population  remains a challenge as cities become  denser  there is increasing pressure on urban  green spaces  each eu citizen throws out nearly half a  ton  of municipal waste every year  inefficient waste management  means that significant quantities of  resources are lost  hindering the transition to a more  circular economy  environmental noise is a growing problem  at least 20 percent of the eu's  population  live in areas where traffic noise levels  are harmful to their health  the green city accord is a movement of  european city leaders with a common  vision  of making their cities clean and healthy  by the year 2030.  joining the accord means a commitment to  significant improvements in five  environmental areas  air quality quality of water bodies and  water use efficiency  urban biodiversity and urban ecosystems  waste management and the circular  economy  and combating noise pollution  in turn cities signing up for the green  city accord will enjoy a number of  benefits  locally they will increase their  credibility in the eyes of their  communities  by becoming more transparent and more  accountable  they will form part of a growing network  of like-minded cities  and be invited to capacity building  activities at the european level their  environmental achievements will become  more visible  let's make our cities greener cleaner  and healthier together  join the green city accord
 

